<title>RUSSIA: FORECAST-Russia 1996 year-on-year inflation 22 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Russia 1996 year-on-year inflation 22 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's 1996 year-on-year inflation will fall to between 22 and 23 percent from 130 percent in 1995, Prime-Tass news agency quoted Economy Minister Yevgeny Yasin as saying on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Year-on-year inflation could fall to between eight to nine percent by the end of 2000, Yasin told a conference on light industry.</p>
<p>Monthly inflation in October was 1.2 percent after 4.1 percent in January.</p>
<p>--Julie Tolkacheva, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
